# Executable API examples for the "REST Client" VS Code extension (humao.rest-client).

@host = http://127.0.0.1:8000/api/v1
@json = application/json

### Register a new user (returns a token too)
# @name register
POST {{host}}/register
Content-Type: {{json}}
Accept: {{json}}

{
  "name": "Ada Lovelace",
  "email": "ada@example.com",
  "password": "secret-password"
}

### Log in with the seeded demo user
# @name login
POST {{host}}/login
Content-Type: {{json}}
Accept: {{json}}

{
  "email": "test@example.com",
  "password": "password"
}

###
@token = {{login.response.body.$.data.token}}

### List my books (offset pagination, default order: newest first)
GET {{host}}/books
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: {{json}}

### Search, sort and choose the page size
GET {{host}}/books?search=a&sort=value&direction=asc&per_page=5
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: {{json}}

### Cursor pagination: follow links.next from the response for the following page
GET {{host}}/books?pagination=cursor&per_page=2
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: {{json}}

### Create a book (only "name" is required)
# @name createBook
POST {{host}}/books
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{json}}
Accept: {{json}}

{
  "name": "Clean Code",
  "isbn": "9780132350884",
  "value": 49.90
}

###
@bookId = {{createBook.response.body.$.data.id}}

### Show it
GET {{host}}/books/{{bookId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: {{json}}

### PATCH: partial update, only the fields sent change
PATCH {{host}}/books/{{bookId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{json}}
Accept: {{json}}

{
  "value": 39.90
}

### PUT: full replacement, every field must be present (null clears isbn/value)
PUT {{host}}/books/{{bookId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{json}}
Accept: {{json}}

{
  "name": "Clean Code, 2nd printing",
  "isbn": "9780132350884",
  "value": null
}

### Delete it
DELETE {{host}}/books/{{bookId}}
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: {{json}}

### Log out (revokes only this token)
POST {{host}}/logout
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: {{json}}

### ---- Error cases ----

### 422: isbn must be 10 or 13 digits
POST {{host}}/books
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Content-Type: {{json}}
Accept: {{json}}

{
  "name": "Bad isbn",
  "isbn": "not-digits"
}

### 401: no token (still JSON, even without an Accept header)
GET {{host}}/books

### 404: a book that is not yours looks exactly like one that does not exist
GET {{host}}/books/999999
Authorization: Bearer {{token}}
Accept: {{json}}
